### Page 2 of 5

```text
Award Information
  Federal Award Identification Number:  WY-2023-004-00
  Award Name:  FY19, FY20, FY21 Section 5307 Operating
  Award Start Date:  7/18/2023
  Original Award End Date:  7/31/2026
  Current Award End Date:  7/31/2026
  Award Executive Summary:  This grant applies for Section 5307 formula funds totaling
$2,418,763 in the following amounts: $53,561 in remaining FFY 2019 funds, $1,180,828
in FFY 2020 funds (the full apportionment), and $1,184,374 in FFY 2021 funds (the full
apportionment).

Projects in this application include:

1. Operating assistance totaling $1,945,724, at a cost-sharing ratio of 50/50.

2. Funds for ADA paratransit operating assistance total $473,039, at a cost-sharing ratio
of 80/20. The total is made up of 20% of the amount of the FY2020 apportionment
($236,165) plus 20% of the FY 2021 apportionment ($236,874). In order to apply for the
20% amount, the City commits to providing a fixed-route travel training program and all
fixed-route operators will participate in passenger safety, disability awareness, and
sensitivity training.

Local funds will be provided by local general funds and non-federal state funds.

Pre-award authority is requested starting 4/1/2023 for $1,945,724 for regular operating
expenses.

Required documentation is attached to the application, including the Governor's
apportionment letters and TIP/STIP documentation.

The Safety and Security requirements will not be met with funding from this application,
as these requirements are being covered by the City's Police and Fire Departments with
funding outside of this application.
  Research and Development:  This award does not include research and development
activities.
  Indirect Costs:  This award is applying an approved Indirect cost rate(s).
```

